nthesis of stalked brush border membrane proteins: Glycosidases and peptidases of enterocytes and renal tubuli</article-title><source>Annu Rev Cell Biol</source><year>1986</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>255</fpage><lpage>313</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1146/annurev.cb.02.110186.001351</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Semenza G. Anchoring and biosynthesis of stalked brush border membrane proteins: Glycosidases and peptidases of enterocytes and renal tubuli. Annu Rev Cell Biol 1986; 2: 255&#x02013;313. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3548768</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>North</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Families of ion channels with two hydrophobic segments</article-title><source>Curr Opin Cell Biol</source><year>1996</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>474</fpage><lpage>483</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0955-0674(96)80023-8</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">North RA. Families of ion channels with two hydrophobic segments. Curr Opin Cell Biol 1996; 8: 474&#x02013;83. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8791456</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Plesner</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ecto-ATPases: Identities and functions</article-title><source>Int Rev Cytol</source><year>1995</year><volume>158</volume><fpage>141</fpage><lpage>214</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0074-7696(08)62487-0</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Plesner L. Ecto-ATPases: Identities and functions. Int Rev Cytol 1995; 158: 141&#x02013;214. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7721538</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>TF</given-names></name><name><surname>Guidotti</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>CD39 is an ecto-(Ca2+, Mg2+)-apyrase</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>1996</year><volume>271</volume><fpage>9898</fpage><lpage>9901</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1074/jbc.271.17.9898</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Wang TF, Guidotti G. CD39 is an ecto-(Ca2+, Mg2+)-apyrase. J Biol Chem 1996; 271: 9898&#x02013;901. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8626624</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maliszewski</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Delespesse</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Schoenborn</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The CD39 lymphoid cell activation antigen. Molecular cloning and structural characterization</article-title><source>J Immunol</source><year>1994</year><volume>153</volume><fpage>3574</fpage><lpage>3583</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Maliszewski CR, Delespesse GJ, Schoenborn MA et al. The CD39 lymphoid cell activation antigen. Molecular cloning and structural characterization. J Immunol 1994; 153: 3574&#x02013;83. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7930580</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>TF</given-names></name><name><surname>Ou</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Guidotti</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The transmembrane domains of ectoapyrase (CD39) affect its enzymatic activity and quaternary structure</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>1998</year><volume>273</v